  {
   "id": 17,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 4707,
   "end": 4722,
   "text": "## Installation",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 18,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 4724,
   "end": 5026,
   "text": "VLABench is **not on PyPI** — its only distribution is the [OpenMOSS/VLABench](⟦0⟧) GitHub repo — so LeRobot does not expose a ⟦1⟧ extra. Install it manually as an editable clone, alongside the MuJoCo / dm_control pins VLABench needs, then fetch the mesh assets:",
   "tokens": [
    "https://github.com/OpenMOSS/VLABench",
    "`vlabench`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 19,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 5448,
   "end": 5572,
   "text": "⟦0⟧\nVLABench requires Linux (⟦1⟧) and Python 3.10+. Set the MuJoCo rendering backend before running:",
   "tokens": [
    "<Tip>",
    "`sys_platform == 'linux'`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 20,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 5653,
   "end": 5666,
   "text": "## Evaluation",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 21,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 5668,
   "end": 5988,
   "text": "All eval snippets below mirror the command CI runs (see ⟦0⟧). The ⟦1⟧ argument maps VLABench's ⟦2⟧ / ⟦3⟧ / ⟦4⟧ camera keys onto the three-camera (⟦5⟧ / ⟦6⟧ / ⟦7⟧) input layout the released ⟦8⟧ policy was trained on.",
   "tokens": [
    "`.github/workflows/benchmark_tests.yml`",
    "`--rename_map`",
    "`image`",
    "`second_image`",
    "`wrist_image`",
    "`camera1`",
    "`camera2`",
    "`camera3`",
    "`smolvla_vlabench`"
   ]
  },
  {
